Database file: ./data/auction.db. main.ts opens process.env.DB_PATH ?? './data/auction.db'.

The browser page public/index.html is the client component WebClient (DSN-042, REQ-001 REQ-002 REQ-003 REQ-004 REQ-005 REQ-008 REQ-009 REQ-012). The first line in <head> of public/index.html is <!-- @trace DSN-042 REQ-001 REQ-002 REQ-003 REQ-004 REQ-005 REQ-008 REQ-009 REQ-012 -->.

Service nodes, each its own process; a class is created only on its own node:
- API Server (DSN-001), primary: entry src/app/main.ts with createApp in src/app/app.ts, port process.env.PORT ?? 8080, classes User (DSN-014), Item (DSN-015), Bid (DSN-016), ItemView (DSN-017), UserController (DSN-018), ItemController (DSN-019), BidController (DSN-020), UserService (DSN-021), ItemService (DSN-022), BidService (DSN-023), AuctionCloser (DSN-024), UserStore (DSN-028), ItemStore (DSN-029), AuctionEventPublisher (DSN-030), BidEventPublisher (DSN-031), EventFeed (DSN-034), Currency (DSN-012), AuctionStatus (DSN-013), PublicItem (DSN-044), ExchangeRateService (DSN-025), FrankfurterClient (DSN-026), opens the database.
  Incoming from Browser (DSN-006) over http: the page and the /api routes.
  Incoming from Live Update Server (DSN-002) over ws: a ws endpoint at /internal/live-update-server; for each message it calls this node's classes, or, for a feed, this node sends its events to every connected socket.
  Outgoing to Frankfurter API (DSN-005) over https: its client class calls it.
- Live Update Server (DSN-002): entry src/app/live-update-server.ts, port process.env.LIVE_UPDATE_SERVER_PORT ?? 8081, classes EventFeedClient (DSN-032), LiveGateway (DSN-033), opens no database.
  Incoming from Browser (DSN-006) over ws: a ws endpoint at / that the page opens at the URL GET /api/config names; it sends to the connected sockets.
  Outgoing to API Server (DSN-001) over ws: its client class reads the URL in its own code from process.env.API_SERVER_URL ?? 'ws://localhost:8080', path /internal/live-update-server.

The primary node serves GET /api/config with { "live-update-server": process.env.LIVE_UPDATE_SERVER_PUBLIC_URL ?? 'ws://localhost:8081' }; the page reads it before it opens the connection.

The page talks to API Server (DSN-001) over http and to Live Update Server (DSN-002) over ws.

Declaration shapes of the changed and added classes, to match exactly; the constructor parameters are fixed:
Item (DSN-015):
export class Item {
  constructor(public id: string, public sellerId: string, public title: string, public startingPrice: number, public reservePrice: number | null, public currency: Currency, public endTime: Date, public status: AuctionStatus, public highestBidAmount: number | null, public highestBidderId: string | null, public winnerId: string | null);
  isOpen(now: Date): boolean;
  minimumBid(): number;
  extendIfLate(now: Date): boolean;
  recordBid(bidderId: string, amount: number): void;
  isReserveMet(): boolean | null;
  close(): void;
}

ItemView (DSN-017):
export interface ItemView {
  item: PublicItem;
  displayCurrency: Currency | null;
  convertedStartingPrice: number | null;
  convertedHighestBid: number | null;
}

ItemController (DSN-019):
export class ItemController {
  constructor(private readonly itemService: ItemService, private readonly exchangeRateService: ExchangeRateService);
  listItem(userId: string, title: string, startingPrice: number, endTime: string, currency: string, reservePrice: number | null): Promise<PublicItem>;
  getItem(id: string, displayCurrency: string | undefined): Promise<ItemView>;
  listOpenItems(): Promise<PublicItem[]>;
}

ItemService (DSN-022):
export class ItemService {
  constructor(private readonly itemStore: ItemStore, private readonly userStore: UserStore, private readonly auctionEventPublisher: AuctionEventPublisher);
  listItem(sellerId: string, title: string, startingPrice: number, endTime: Date, currency: string, reservePrice: number | null): Promise<PublicItem>;
  getItem(id: string): Promise<PublicItem>;
  listOpenItems(): Promise<PublicItem[]>;
  closeDueAuctions(now: Date): Promise<void>;
}

BidService (DSN-023):
export class BidService {
  constructor(private readonly itemStore: ItemStore, private readonly bidEventPublisher: BidEventPublisher, private readonly userStore: UserStore);
  placeBid(itemId: string, bidderId: string, amount: number): Promise<Bid>;
}

ItemStore (DSN-029):
export class ItemStore {
  constructor(db: DatabaseSync);
  saveItem(item: Item): Promise<Item>;
  findItem(id: string): Promise<Item | null>;
  findOpenItems(): Promise<Item[]>;
  findDueItems(now: Date): Promise<Item[]>;
  saveBid(bid: Bid): Promise<Bid>;
}

AuctionEventPublisher (DSN-030):
export class AuctionEventPublisher {
  constructor(private readonly eventFeed: EventFeed);
  publishAuctionClosed(item: Item): Promise<void>;
}

BidEventPublisher (DSN-031):
export class BidEventPublisher {
  constructor(private readonly eventFeed: EventFeed);
  publishBidAccepted(bid: Bid, item: Item): Promise<void>;
}

LiveGateway (DSN-033):
export class LiveGateway {
  constructor(public sockets: Map<string, WebSocket>);
  watch(clientId: string, itemId: string): void;
  unwatch(clientId: string, itemId: string): void;
  broadcast(itemId: string, message: string): void;
}

PublicItem (DSN-044):
export interface PublicItem {
  id: string;
  sellerId: string;
  title: string;
  startingPrice: number;
  currency: Currency;
  endTime: Date;
  status: AuctionStatus;
  highestBidAmount: number | null;
  highestBidderId: string | null;
  winnerId: string | null;
  reserveMet: boolean | null;
}

Patch only the files these IDs involve, then run typecheck and detect_drift and fix until both are clean.
